cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this study or its supporting code, please cite both the OSF pre-registration and the archived release of this repository."
type: software
title: "energy-proxy: SCED rebaseline analysis stack for a single-household HVAC controller field study"
abstract: >
  Real-time and historical residential energy monitoring with dynamic-pricing-aware
  HVAC scheduling, plus the analysis pipeline that supports a pre-registered
  single-case experimental design (SCED) field study comparing the CTK04AE
  thermostat's programmed schedule (Arm A) against the active hvac-scheduler
  controller (Arm B: RTP/DTOD/5CP-risk-aware RBC with safety supervisor).
  Conducted as building-as-subject measurement by an unaffiliated owner-investigator
  in a single Plainfield, IL household over the 2026 cooling season (2026-06-01
  through 2026-11-16, 12 arm periods of 14 days each).
authors:
